cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ApexTrace: driving signatures from low-rate public Formula 1 telemetry"
authors:
  - family-names: Zaman
    given-names: Sadman
    affiliation: "Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology (BUET)"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SadMan-ZaMaN/ApexTrace"
abstract: >-
  A signal-processing study of public Formula 1 timing data (about 3.77 samples per
  second): measurement error of corner features on synthetic laps, a track coordinate
  from a complementary filter, corner features for every qualifying session of
  2023-2025, and preregistered tests of repeatability, teammate identification on
  held-out sessions, and whether a driving signature follows a driver to a new team.
keywords:
  - signal processing
  - telemetry
  - Formula 1
  - driver identification
  - preregistration
